From c868734905b8947966625065932e692a9527b72d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:20:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [DVBridge] Low-Latency shows no metadata as sent while
 something is drawn over it

Low-Latency carries no Dolby Vision metadata in the picture: Prepare()
leaves the blocks sent to the display unread for it (sentCount -1), so
the rows "Sent to the TV", "Blocks sent", "Not sent" and "L5 sent" of
the player information stay hidden. Pack() read them back a second time
for a frame with something drawn over the picture (the level 5 block
taken out to what covers the bars), and that read did not look at
Low-Latency. The player information is itself drawn over the picture,
so while it was open in Low-Latency it showed the blocks of the RPU as
sent to the TV (issue #25: "L1, L2 x3, L4, L5" on a projector in
Low-Latency).

The second read is now skipped in Low-Latency too, as the first is.
Native Standard output is unchanged.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.cpp
index e27a285..b191610 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.cpp
@@ -1811,8 +1811,10 @@ bool CDVBridgeGLES::Pack(unsigned int framebuffer, int width, int height, bool f
     }
   }
   // Hades: what of the metadata the display is sent, read back again: the level 5 block may have
-  // been taken out to what was drawn over the bars
-  if (cover != Cover::NONE && m_pendingDetail.valid)
+  // been taken out to what was drawn over the bars. (Low-Latency sends no metadata, as Prepare()
+  // says: nothing of it is shown as sent, also while something is drawn over the picture, such
+  // as the player information itself)
+  if (cover != Cover::NONE && m_pendingDetail.valid && !m_lowLatencyOn)
   {
     const auto* candidate = dvbridge_render_candidate(m_renderer);
     unsigned int area[4], margins[4];
-- 
